WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.450
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
features some very high-profile deaths.

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.130
Whether it was a famous mutant or a superhuman
king who lives on the moon, here is every

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.099
superhero that died in "Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness."

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.030
Not even Doctor Strange himself makes it out
alive of "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.030
of Madness."

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:25.230
Although it wasn't the Earth-616 version of
Stephen Strange who ultimately met his maker,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.270
but several variants.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:31.080
That said, the main universe's sorcerer must
be looking over his shoulder a lot more after

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.820
witnessing his Multiverse selves crumble before
his eyes.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.559
Right at the start of "The Multiverse of Madness,"
a Strange variant bites the dust after a fight

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:41.140
with a demonic creature.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.249
His body is then transported to Earth-616.

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:48.890
Eventually, his corpse ends up becoming a
reanimated zombie used to stop the Scarlet

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.120
Witch in the finale.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.820
"I don't even wanna know!"

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:58.829
A flashback also showed how Earth-838's Strange
was obliterated by Black Bolt after becoming

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:00.339
too obsessed with the Darkhold.

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:05.410
Then, to solidify the belief that all bad
things happen in threes, the 616 Strange had

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.320
to put a stop to Sinister Strange.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.400
After all the disappointment and hurt suffered
in her early years, it appeared as if Wanda

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.150
Maximoff had found her own ray of sunshine
in the form of Vision and the Avengers after

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.840
the events of "Age of Ultron."

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.870
But it wasn't meant to be as Thanos' power
ripped away everything that mattered to her.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:28.640
The suffering this caused trapped her in a
darkness that gave rise to the Scarlet Witch,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.960
one of the most powerful beings on Earth.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.450
Scarlet Witch was responsible for the deaths
of nearly everyone on this list as she tried

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.960
to create her own perfect reality.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.590
In the end, though, she realized that her
methods had turned her into the kind of monster

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:42.890
she despised.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.430
Faced with what she had become, she destroyed
the Darkhold in every universe and destroyed

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:51.550
the ruins of Mount Wundagore, burying herself
under the rubble.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:55.670
There's no guarantee that Wanda is well and
truly gone since this is the comic book movie

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.460
world and deaths are about as permanent as
rub-on tattoos.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.780
If this was her last appearance, though, at
least she died as a hero and not the villain.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.870
Comic book movies can be extremely cruel.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:11.390
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
marked the third time that we witnessed Patrick

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.670
Stewart's Charles Xavier die onscreen.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:18.750
First, we watched him be vaporized by Jean
Grey in "X-Men: The Last Stand," then he made

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.239
us all bawl our eyes out as he met his demise
in "Logan," and now this?

00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:27.189
Professor X is quickly becoming the Sean Bean
of superhero films.

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:31.200
Much like his other portrayals, Xavier was
prepared to die for what he believed in "The

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.659
Multiverse of Madness."

00:02:32.659 --> 00:02:36.269
While the rest of the Illuminati wanted to
stop the Scarlet Witch through the threat

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:37.269
of violence.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:41.569
Charles tried to reach out to Wanda through
her mind and reason with the troubled magic

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:42.569
user.

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:46.500
What he found was the real Wanda trapped away
in her mind as the Scarlet Witch took over

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.500
her body.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.840
Professor X was also close to liberating her
from the power of the Darkhold.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.920
The Scarlet Witch proved to be too powerful
for him in the end and snapped his neck in

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.099
the psychic world.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:02.370
Sadly, the consequences of this violent act
were fatal in the conscious world as well.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:08.090
Marvel fans received a memorable MCU moment
as Lashana Lynch's Maria Rambeau appeared

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:12.580
as Captain Marvel, dispelling all theories
that it was Tom Cruise as the Invincible Iron

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.189
Man in the trailer footage.

00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:19.109
However, this was Earth-838's version of the
character, not the main universe's Captain

00:03:19.109 --> 00:03:22.440
Marvel, who is presumably still Carol Danvers.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:27.629
It was a nice tribute to Maria, who was introduced
as Danvers' best friend and went on to found

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:29.939
the alien-intelligence agency S.W.O.R.D.

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:34.829
Plus, it laid an excellent foundation for
"The Marvels," as Maria's daughter, Monica,

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:37.310
developed cosmic powers in "WandaVision."

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.930
Unfortunately, Captain Marvel flew too close
to the sun in "The Multiverse of Madness"

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.849
as Scarlet Witch crushed her with a giant
pillar.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:49.819
While Maria's powers were as impressive and
fiery as expected, she was no match for Wanda

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:50.819
in the battle.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:54.580
Out of all of the Illuminati members, she
was the one who put up the most resistance,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:59.950
but her biggest failure was the same as the
others: They underestimated just how powerful

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.810
the Scarlet Witch really was.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.890
Sometimes, trailers spoil the biggest surprises.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.749
"The Illuminati will see you now."

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:11.519
That's what happened in the case of "Doctor
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:16.030
Many fans predicted the arrival of Captain
Carter in the movie, thanks to one of the

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.500
final trailers that showed off the iconic
shield.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:23.050
It wasn't the first time that we saw Peggy
Carter as the super-soldier, as she flung

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.900
the mighty shield in "What If... ?" as well.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.750
That said, there was something special about
seeing Hayley Atwell's Captain Carter in live-action.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:35.400
While Earth-838's Cap put up a valiant fight
against Scarlet Witch and even uttered the

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.230
unforgettable "I can do this all day" phrase,
the shield ended up being her downfall.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.850
It worked well as a weapon when Cap flung
it around and used it to bounce off enemies

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:48.660
and walls, but it also demonstrated how dangerous
it could be if it wasn't caught on time.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:54.010
Let's put it this way: After this incident,
there were two Caps in Earth-838 and neither

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.800
of them was much for fighting.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.060
The only good news is Captain Carter will
still show up in future episodes of "What If... ?"

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.296
It finally happened!

00:05:03.296 --> 00:05:07.830
The casting that every MCU fan demanded: "The
Office" star John Krasinski as Reed Richards.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:13.169
For years, Fantastic Four fans have wondered
when and how Marvel's First Family would debut

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:17.860
in the shared cinematic universe, and the
answer arrived emphatically in "Doctor Strange

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.639
in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:24.430
The stretchy superhero appeared as part of
the Illuminati and did his best to halt Scarlet

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:30.080
Witch in her tracks, but Wanda turned Mister
Fantastic into her own personal Play-Doh and

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.560
ended his brief appearance in the movie.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.639
Expectedly, many fans are wondering if this
will be a one-and-done deal for Krasinski's

00:05:36.639 --> 00:05:38.190
Richards in the MCU.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.740
Considering how vocal the people have been
about this casting in the past and how well-received

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:47.159
it was by the general audience, it would feel
like a missed opportunity if Marvel Studios

00:05:47.159 --> 00:05:52.190
didn't introduce Krasinski as Earth-616's
Mister Fantastic as well.

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:56.530
The only question is, who will be making up
the remaining members of the Fantastic Four?

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.759
Maybe his wife, Emily Blunt, might suit up
as Susan Storm, even if she claims to not

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.110
be interested in superhero movies.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.280
"Come find me when you wake u-"

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:11.780
While ABC's "Inhumans" series was far from
a resounding success and constantly cited

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:16.990
as one of the MCU's biggest misses, Anson
Mount's Black Bolt received a chance at redemption

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.409
in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:06:19.409 --> 00:06:24.569
Introduced in a comics-accurate costume and
as a member of the Illuminati, he only showed

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:26.500
up for a brief moment in the film.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:30.789
However, it was arguably a much better depiction
of the character than the first time we met

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:34.370
the big shot of Attilan in the 2017 television
show.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:39.120
While fans found out how destructive a whisper
from Black Bolt can be and Reed Richards threatened

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.400
to unleash him on Scarlet Witch if she didn't
back down, the Inhuman's death quickly became

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.150
an online meme after the film's release.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:50.870
Wanda magically stitched up Black Bolt's mouth,
causing him to panic, make the slightest of

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.550
peeps, and blow up his own head.

